{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>I am with you.</b> Because he was afraid of Esav and of Lavan." "<b>Until I have done.</b> אִם functions in the sense of כִּי (Gittin 90a)." "<b>What I spoke to you.</b> For your needs and concerning you. What I promised Abraham concerning his seed — to you I promised it, and not to Esav. For I did not say to him כִּי יִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זֶרַע — but rather כִּי בְיִצְחָק, and not all of Yitzchak. And so too all instances of לִי, לְךָ, לוֹ, לָהֶם adjacent to speech function in the sense of עַל. And this proves it — for with Ya'akov He had not spoken beforehand."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:57.648366539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}